  "text": "Recipe: Moong Masoor Cookies\nCreator: Mrs N K Manku\nCategory: Cookies\nIngredients: green moong daal, red masoor daal, rolled oats, flaxseed powder, Garlic Herb Bread spice mix, garlic, paprika, onion, oregano, basil, thyme, red pepper, marjoram\nCooking methods: soak, ferment, grind, mix, air-fry, bake\nInstructions: Soak overnight: 1 cup green moong daal and 1 cup red masoor daal. Next day, drain the water & ferment for 8 hours. Grind them together into a batter. Add 1 cup rolled oats, 1 Tbsp flaxseed powder and 1 tsp Garlic Herb Bread spice mix (garlic, paprika, onion, oregano, basil, thyme, red pepper, marjoram). Mix all the ingredients into a batter. Make small balls. Sprinkle some rolled oats on top. Press them in (see pic). Bake in an air fryer for 20 mins at 180 C. Then flip them over and air fry for another 10 mins.\nNotes: A recipe with WHOLE GRAINS (rolled oats), BEANS (green moong dal, red masoor dal), NUTS & SEEDS (flaxseed powder), HERBS & SPICES (Garlic Herb Bread spice mix).",
